Honestly, most of these would wash over me. I'd still be grabbing whatever's reduced on the shelf that afternoon, and the price sticker matters more to me than any label.

The graphic ones (B and E) would just make me roll my eyes. A bowel tumour on a packet of Doritos? It's the same tone they always use, like I've never heard of a biscuit. Though if the calorie number's right there in big letters, I might glance at it, especially next to a fruit pot at 95. I don't count, but I'd notice a 240 next to a 95. That's the bit I could imagine nudging me, so D gets the most points. The text-only warning (F) I'd skip entirely. I'd read the first two words and move on.


