Honestly, most of these would wash over me. The photos in A and B would probably make me wince and then feel talked down to, like a dentist's waiting room poster. I'd notice the shock, but I'd resent it more than I'd change my order. The plain text warnings in D and F are just packaging noise to me. I'd read "excess calories" and think, yeah, obviously.

The calorie number is the only bit that might actually register. If a Dairy Milk says 240 and a fruit pot says 95, I might think twice, especially on a skint week. I don't count calories, but a number is quick and doesn't make me feel judged. Price would still beat it, though. A fruit pot costs more than I want to pay for something that's not filling. So the calorie badge gets most of my points, and the graphic warnings barely move me.

