Honestly, most of these would wash over me. I'm not counting calories, and I buy what looks good on the walk back. The scary pictures and warnings feel like being told off, and I'd probably roll my eyes and grab the shortbread anyway. Plain text warnings are even easier to ignore because they're just nagging.

The calorie badge on its own is the only one that's actually useful. If the Dairy Milk says 240 and the fruit pot says 95, that's a fact I can use without being lectured. Even so, I'd only notice it now and then, and I still wouldn't always pick the healthier one.

