Honestly, most of these would wash over me. I'm not counting calories. I'm working out what fits the budget and what I can eat after a 12-miler. A calorie badge on the Dairy Milk might make me pause for a second, and I'd probably think "fair enough, I'm training," then buy it anyway. The bowel-cancer photo is the sort of thing I'd scroll past, like the stuff on Facebook. It's trying to frighten me, and that just puts my back up. The plain text warning is slightly better, but it's still the "you've failed" tone I can't stand.

Only the calorie numbers next to a warning would give me something to think about. Even then it'd be the lower-calorie fruit pot being cheaper and nicer after a run, not the scare.

